Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.990 align:start position:0%
 
the world of elden ring is full of  interesting mysteries it's how the game  was designed and how from software  designs all of their games they use  environmental storytelling to have the  players and the community make theories  on what certain things mean and what  they connect to the lore of elden ring  was and still is being heavily  researched and theories are coming out  like wildfire from so many amazing  creators and enthusiasts of the game so  much so that it's overwhelming to put  all of that information together into a  somewhat understandable plot line while  the main aspects of the story are pretty  clear to understand the details of the  world that we'll talk about in this  video will definitely lead to more  questions than answers so let's take a  look at some interesting finds together  and we'll discuss in the comments what  we think they could mean some of these  finds are just interesting and really  have nothing to do with the story but  some of them could lead to connections  within the story if you have any  interesting finds that you'd like to  point out you can join our discord and  discuss it there you can message me on  twitter or instagram or again just  comment down below so let's get into it  the first thing i'd like to discuss are  the isolated towers most people have  found that when observed from the map or  from the sky the towers create a circle  when linked together but when looking at  the outside of each tower you'll notice  that the left side is sort of distorted  i originally thought that this distorted  side of the tower pointed toward pharam  azula but that doesn't seem to be  consistent with all of the towers there  also seems to be a missing tower located  near the capital city the lead up in  entrance through this area is almost  exactly similar to that of other divine  tower locations however that path  abruptly ends sort of like it was  scraped completely off of the hill this  could be the original location of the  isolated tower and from this tower  pharam azula can be seen out in the  distance it is known that pharah  missoula used to hover above limgrave  and stormville castle where missoula  then moved out to the far east maybe the  tornado ripped off the isolated tower  and then somehow placed it in the middle  of the sea on its way to its present  location or this could have been the  location of mykola's divine tower that  we currently don't know the location of  yet although what's more likely is that  mykola and melania share a divine tower  since they're twins just like morgot and  moog also regarding pharaoh missoula i  thought it was somewhat interesting that  the layout of pharamizula is the same  from a distance as it is when we are  actually there i've had a theory that  pharaoh missoula when we are sent there  is outside the present time of when we  are in the lands between throughout the  rest of the game even if that may or may  not be the case the layout is the same  not rendered very well obviously but we  can see the great bridge leading up to  malachite's boss room i've also been  spending a lot of time listening to  certain sound effects throughout the  game i've literally been running around  playing the game with only sound effects  turned all the way up with everything  else turned down the most interesting  sound i've heard so far is from the  elden beast which gives off a very  distinct bass boosted sound that gives  me vibes of interstellar space which  fits the theme of the boss perfectly  take a listen  now i'm sure this has already been seen  or mentioned somewhere out there but the  elden beast character model goes far  below the boss arena with a very long  tail that has some golden roots growing  off the end of it this is obviously for  when it leaps up into the air but i  found it interesting that they kept that  part of the model fully rendered at all  times small but weird find for this area  as well is if we move the camera far  above the arena we can see the platform  that we fight against ratagon on still  somewhat rendered in along with a fully  rendered summoning pool the door to the  er tree and a fog gate they likely have  to keep these assets rendered in if the  player does use the summoning pool to  fight with a friend as for the fog gate  and the door i have no idea why these  are here another interesting find about  melania is that she is more than likely  most definitely blind when we enter the  boss room before triggering the cutscene  we can see a really good look at how  badly her eyes have just been completely  taken over by the scarlet rot i'm not  entirely sure why it looks so much worse  here than it does in the cutscenes  probably because it's not fully rendered  because the player would never be able  to get in this position without the help  of mods like i'm doing here so they  probably just didn't need to render it  her blindness could explain why her  waterfowl dance is her just flirting  around randomly it's not like she's  panicking but it's like she doesn't know  our exact location so she flurries her  sword around seemingly at random to have  a better chance at hitting us and that  seems to work just fine for her most of  the time she's likely tracking us  through the rest of the fight based on  the sounds we make in the water and just  in the boss room all together next thing  i want to talk about are the cut scenes  for most boss fights in the game if you  didn't know the cutscenes are generated  within the game they position the  player's character model in certain  positions and based on the scene the  developers want it to show they'll move  the characters around to get the best  shot for the camera sometimes they'll  just remove the player's character model  altogether since they're just not in the  shot for that scene they'll also  sometimes move models in certain  positions floating above the ground just  to get a better shot they'll also change  the lighting around for what works  better within the frame of that shot i  find all this stuff really interesting  for some reason as it dives into the  critical thinking process of the  developers and what they were trying to  showcase for certain scenes and boss  fights they'll even blur the entire  surrounding area when the shot is close  up to a character model which gives a  sense of depth to the shot that would  otherwise look a bit strange without the  blurred background the melania boss  fight has a lot of cool examples of this  like i've been showing on screen now i  didn't notice this next find till  recently but you can see that surash  godfrey's lion companion is actually  biting down on godfrey's shoulder during  the first phase of the boss fight suraj  is meant to calm godfrey when he's  fighting so he doesn't abandon his elden  lord status to fight like the warrior he  truly is like he does in the second  phase so it's interesting to see this  calming effect is just the form of suraj  biting down on godfrey another small  note is that godfrey isn't actually  holding morgot in his arms until the cut  scene actually starts they probably  didn't think it relevant to do so since  he has his back turned to us and  wouldn't be in the view of the player  till the cutscene actually starts also  when we zoom in close on godfrey's eyes  we can see that they're faded out and to  me resembled the faded dead eyes of  godwin in the deep root depths we know  that godfrey's sight of grace was taken  away by queen merika and it's possible  his eyes used to have this golden hue  just like when we look into the eyes of  godric who is another descendant of the  golden lineage of godfrey himself and  while we're on the topic of eyes when we  look closely at gideon's armor set the  eyes throughout the set also have  similarities to that of godwin the armor  set has that same gray faded out hue to  that of godwin's eyes it's also known  that godwin's influence even with the  death of his soul his body is still  spreading throughout the lands between  we can see godwin's eyes in so many  different places and when we think of  gideon being the all-knowing it would  sort of make sense that he'd want eyes  all over the world to gain as much  knowledge as possible this is obviously  a bit of a stretch but nonetheless is  still an interesting theory last thing i  want to talk about today was an  interesting find found by a souls  creator  zolly the witch but in regards to radon  she found that when you look below the  boss arena when radon leaps into the sky  he plunges his horse leonard below the  sand you can actually see that leonard  tracks your location  under the sand so that radon's character  model knows where to crash down at the  start of his second phase this is  definitely one of the coolest finds i've  found in the game so far also when it  comes to radon i'm sure it's already  widely known that radon doesn't have  feet they've either fallen off from the  spread of the scarlet rot or scraped off  when he drags his feet through the sand  for what is likely thousands of years  but if we look a bit closer we can  definitely see a type of fungus  surrounding the legs that doesn't have  that red hue that is normally  representing the scarlet rot there's  also some type of webbing connection  with the fungus as well no idea what  this could be at this time but let me  know what you think and that goes for  everything we've discussed in this video  and again you can join our discord and  message me on twitter instagram if  there's certain interesting findings  that you've found and want to discuss  shout out to my patrons with the  continued support they get early access  to videos with absolutely no ads so if  you're interested in that check the  links down below also i've started a  second channel called agt golf where i  want to start making golf content i  haven't talked about this too much on  this channel but i used to be a  professional golfer and unfortunately  suffered nerve damage in my right wrist  i haven't played competitively in a few  years but my wrist feels great and  thanks to you guys i'm now in a position  to work from home and have a lot of time  to practice so if you guys are  interested in some different content  from myself go check out my golf channel  linked in the description i'll start  putting out some videos there whenever i  figure out the best way to do so  appreciate all of you guys very much  thanks for watching the video and i will  see you in the next one take care

